# Which application release each PHP version is tested against.
#
# One row per fixture set. A PHP version resolves, per app, to the one row
# whose [php-min, php-max] range contains it; ranges for an app must not
# overlap and must cover every matrix.json version (lib.sh's `sets check`
# enforces both). The newest release that supports a PHP version wins, so a
# version is always tested against the application its users would actually
# run on it, not the oldest one that still happens to boot.
#
# php-min is also the PHP the fixture is BUILT on: every set is installed,
# composer-resolved and populated on the stock image for php-min
# (APPTEST_BUILDER_REPO, dementev/php-fpm-with-ext by default), so the data
# the from-source images are tested against was written by a known-good PHP
# they have to stay compatible with -- serialized sessions, password hashes,
# cache entries and all.
#
